\newlabel{tab:scannet_published_context}{{IX}{9}{Quantitative evaluation of ScanNet-v2 open-vocabulary point querying on the VALA eight-scene subset. Baselines are published source-paper values, whereas \method {} is our locally auditable direct point-query result. The evaluation domains are not yet unified, so external rows are reported context rather than a strict same-protocol ranking; results are in percent}{table.9}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {X}{\ignorespaces ScanNet VALA8 category stability for the GaussFM{} DINO-CV contextual kNN classifier with spatial logit propagation. Statistics are per-class IoU across scenes where the class appears; ``range'' is min--max IoU.}}{9}{table.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:scannet_category_stability}{{X}{9}{ScanNet VALA8 category stability for the \method {} DINO-CV contextual kNN classifier with spatial logit propagation. Statistics are per-class IoU across scenes where the class appears; ``range'' is min--max IoU}{table.10}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {XI}{\ignorespaces Single-query latency evidence. Lower is better. Values are derived from frozen profile artifacts and are conservative because the profiled commands include evaluator overhead and, for LERF rendered-view runs, visualization/RADIO-target branches. Direct 3D latency includes query-select-render mask generation.}}{9}{table.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:efficiency_cost}{{XI}{9}{Single-query latency evidence. Lower is better. Values are derived from frozen profile artifacts and are conservative because the profiled commands include evaluator overhead and, for LERF rendered-view runs, visualization/RADIO-target branches. Direct 3D latency includes query-select-render mask generation}{table.11}{}}
